# Coding and review standards for this repository.

```yaml
codingStandards:
  languages:
    Python:
      version: "3.12"
      conventions:
        - PEP 8 naming and readable small functions
        - Configuration through environment variables
    Bash:
      conventions:
        - Use set -Eeuo pipefail
        - Quote variable expansions
        - Make deployment idempotent
  frameworks:
    Flask:
      - Use an application factory so tests and Gunicorn share the same setup.
      - Keep routes simple and deterministic.
  testing:
    framework: pytest
    runner: pytest
    location: tests
    requirements:
      - Test all acceptance-critical routes and version rendering.
      - Do not depend on external services in unit tests.
  review:
    dimensions:
      - correctness
      - security
      - maintainability
      - test coverage
      - deployment safety
      - beginner readability
    securityChecks:
      - No hard-coded credentials or private keys
      - Container runs as a non-root user
      - Only necessary ports are exposed
      - GitHub Actions use least-privilege permissions
  entropy:
    removeOnTouch: true
    blockReview:
      - dead code
      - duplicated deployment paths
      - obsolete configuration
      - dangling references
  documentation:
    stackRules: []
    projectGuide: README.md
```
